# Git worktrees of other branches, created by the delivery workflows. Git
# already declines to stage a nested worktree — it sees the `.git` file and
# stops — so `git add -A` was safe without this line. It is here so the intent
# is written down rather than resting on a git behaviour nobody stated, and so
# that a `git add` of a path inside it has to be forced. Never force it: that
# commits another branch's whole tree (#148).
.claude/
